Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:03.99,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Did you know that molecules like to make friends\Njust like you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.99,0:00:04.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}They come together
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.93,0:00:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}change partners
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.72,0:00:06.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}and even take breaks!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.76,0:00:10.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Let me tell you the story of how they do all this
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.45,0:00:10.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}First
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.75,0:00:13.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}imagine two little molecules meeting for the first\Ntime
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.52,0:00:15.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}This is called synthesis
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.52,0:00:18.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}They get together and decide to become one\Nhappy group
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.76,0:00:19.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}just like when two
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.83,0:00:23.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}pieces of a puzzle fit perfectly to make a whole\Npicture
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.21,0:00:24.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}This happens when
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.16,0:00:24.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}for instance
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.84,0:00:26.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}hydrogen and oxygen meet to make water!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.90,0:00:27.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Now
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.11,0:00:29.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}sometimes friends need a little space
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.05,0:00:30.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}In a process called decomposition
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.86,0:00:32.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}a molecule decides to split into two
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.83,0:00:33.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}just
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.04,0:00:37.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}like when you break a cookie into halves to share\Nwith a buddy
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.04,0:00:40.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}This happens when water decides to separate\Nback into hydrogen and oxygen
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.73,0:00:43.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Sometimes molecules like to have a dance party!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.19,0:00:44.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}In single replacement
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.45,0:00:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}one friend steps in to dance with one of the\Npartners
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.49,0:00:48.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}switching places
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.32,0:00:49.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}just like musical chairs
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.49,0:00:53.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}It's like zinc deciding to step in and dance with\Nsome sulfur
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.11,0:00:54.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}leaving copper on
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.10,0:00:56.10,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}its own
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.10,0:00:57.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Then there’s double replacement
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.49,0:00:58.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}where everyone finds new friends
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.87,0:01:01.02,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Imagine two pairs of friends swapping partners
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.02,0:01:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}It’s like a friendship swap where everyone finds\Na new buddy to hang out with
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.63,0:01:09.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}just like silver and chlorine trading partners with\Nsodium and nitrate
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.01,0:01:11.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}There are other exciting things molecules do
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.32,0:01:11.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}too
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.47,0:01:12.73,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Like during combustion
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.73,0:01:15.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}where a fuel burns in the presence of air
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.03,0:01:15.47,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}creating
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.47,0:01:15.88,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}energy
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.88,0:01:18.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}like the warmth you feel from a campfire
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.24,0:01:18.72,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Sometimes
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.72,0:01:21.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}molecules decide to settle down and form\Nsomething solid
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.49,0:01:21.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}like when
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.93,0:01:24.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}raindrops turn into hailstones – that's\Nprecipitation!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.08,0:01:26.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}And let's not forget when acids and bases meet
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.84,0:01:28.32,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}They balance each other out
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.32,0:01:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}forming salt and water
Dialogue: 0,0:01:29.53,0:01:30.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}almost like mixing paints
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.84,0:01:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}to create a new color
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.84,0:01:36.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}Next time you’re playing with friends or\Nbuilding with blocks
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.06,0:01:36.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\alpha&HCC&}think about how
